zig: the prompt cache's keep floor and refused saves

The kept-state budget stopped at MemAvailable - MEMORY_RESERVE_GIB, so the
cache filled to the reserve itself and the next keep took one rank under it:
takeSnap returned BelowMemoryReserve after the ranks had agreed on the keep,
and the agreement made it fatal ("a prompt's prefill failed after the ranks
agreed (BelowMemoryReserve); exiting"). Seen on a TP=2 pair with
--prompt-cache-gib 8 (a 5.3 GiB budget after the reserve) and
TF_GLM_CACHE_ENTRIES=32, after a few hundred prompts.

- cuda_cache_plan: TF_GLM_KEEP_HEADROOM_GIB (2 GiB by default; 0 turns it
  off): what the kept states' budget leaves free above the reserve for the
  prompts' own buffers as they grow. The budget is the asked size, at most
  what is free at start minus the reserve and this headroom; the keep floor
  (where a save is refused) stays the reserve, so a full cache still leaves
  the headroom to the prompts. The startup line says both.
- cuda_lanes pass: before each keep the ranks agree that every rank has room
  for the state (Engine.keepFits, from /proc/meminfo); without it the mark is
  skipped on all ranks. After the keep's prefill the ranks agree on the save's
  outcome too: a save the engine refused on any rank (memory went in between,
  or no device memory) is kept by none, the other rank frees the state it
  took, and every rank goes on from the rows it just ran (`live_from`): no
  restore, no rows twice. A rank keeping alone would be no use: a resume
  needs the state on all ranks, and the ranks' segments must match.
- cuda_engine prefillWith: a refused save keeps nothing and warns instead of
  failing the prefill; `live_from` continues from the sequence's own rows;
  a prefill from the start on a sequence that ran rows zeroes its recurrent
  state first, on the engine's stream (position 0 does not clear it by
  itself). Other errors still fail the prefill.
- cuda_native: with an MTP head loaded the cache stays off (the head's taps
  count from the prompt's start, so a continuation would misplace them; a
  log line says so). The default configuration, DFlash2 drafts without an
  MTP head, is unaffected.
- tests (host, a mock engine under the lanes): the planner's headroom
  (parsing, the floor at an exact fit and one byte under, the budget, the
  launch defaults keep theirs); on two ranks: the room refusal, and one
  rank's late refusal in each direction, with both ranks' segment traces
  equal (every row once), both replies the fresh prompt's, kept lists
  equal, no leaked state; on one rank: the engine's refusal from cold and
  with an earlier state kept (every row once, the reply the fresh one).
  The engine's own `live_from` is beyond the host suite. Live TP=2 runs on
  the image built from this patch (--prompt-cache-gib 8, 32 entries): with
  the default headroom no keep was refused; with the headroom off the room
  check skipped 127 keeps at the reserve and the server ran on; no save was
  refused after the agreement in either, so `live_from` ran only in the
  host tests. Every reply in both runs equals the Python engine's (428
  sweep cases, 56 main-set requests). The cold reset of a used sequence is
  defensive: the lanes never prefill a used sequence from the start (they
  pass `live_from` or `resume_from`), so no path exercises it; it has no
  test.

